	(text "I = 2 mA max\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 146.812 160.528 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "5ca788b0-97fe-41f0-a882-c3cd011e8716")
	)
	(text "SPI flash PROM AT25EU0011A meets all of the requirements in iCE40 Programming and Configuration.\nHowever, will have to hold CRESET_B low until the PROM is ready (~300 us?) (BY25Q40GWTIG(T) is cheaper)\n\nWill also need a USB to SPI (FT2232HPQ supports both UART and SPI at the same time but\ncomes standard with both channels A and B being UART... so need to configure)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -109.474 20.574 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7ca5ebfd-5a2a-467c-8840-4eb98fde2490")
	)
	(text "FPGA uses SPI mode 3 for reading from SPI FLASH."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -85.344 61.722 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "ae6ac080-9f34-484d-b3a5-f1400c4bcd51")
	)
	(text "Let's assume worst case for the FPGA, i.e., 0 lfm. This means thermal resistance is R = 37.1 C/W:\n\nP = T/R = (125C - 20C)/37.1 = 2.83 W => I = 2.83W/1.2V = 2.359 A max\n\nWith GPIO max current draw being 390mA @ 3.3V, the GPIO max power is 1.287W, which means the core can draw\na max of 2.83W - 1.287W = 1.543W => 1.2858A\n\nThe total current drawn by all 3.3V devices is 773.3mA. So, the power supplies should be:\n\n1.2V, 1.2858A minimum\n\n3.3V, 773.3mA minimum"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 462.534 30.734 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b37d4383-7aed-4e21-9875-5d8a7586eb02")
	)
	(text "I = 3 mA max"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 375.666 243.078 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "d0764335-0930-4495-89e7-34db88a7cf9c")
	)
	(text "- See Table 4.2 of iCE40 UltraPlus Family Data Sheet for information regarding power supply voltages"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -110.744 34.29 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f3eb7f89-eebe-4f5e-86de-a0fcf4fa8380")
	)
